data:
{{Top}}
{{Youmay|the type of [[capital ship]]|a specific model, such as the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]]}}
{{Quote|I'm always nervous, seeing Star Destroyers like that. They ain't natural, ships that big.|[[Shawburn]]|<ref name="Rebel Rising">''[[Rebel Rising]]''</ref>}}
[[File:ExecutorEscort-BTMF27.png|thumb|right|250px|The Empire used a number of types of Star Destroyers.]]
A '''Star Destroyer''' was a dagger-shaped type of [[capital ship]] that were used by the [[Galactic Republic]], the [[Galactic Empire]], the [[First Order]], and the [[Sith Eternal]]. Notable examples of Star Destroyers include the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]] and its predecessor, the [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]].<ref name="ISD DB" />

==Characteristics==
===Design===
{{Quote|I thought everything was being dismantled or torched in one star or another. What does anyone need with battle droids when the Empire has Star Destroyers?|Has Obitt, after he heard some [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] supplies were being kept around|<ref name="Catalyst" />}}
According to [[Everi Chalis]], Star Destroyers were the most resource-intensive [[Starship|ships]] [[the galaxy]] had ever seen, and only [[Kuat]] possessed [[Kuat Drive Yards|shipyards]] that were capable of supporting and maintaining more than a handful at a [[time]].<ref name="BF">''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]''</ref>

===Classes===
====Star Dreadnoughts====
[[File:Executor_BF2.png|thumb|left|275px|The ''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought.]]
The ''Executor''-class [[Star Dreadnought]],<ref name="UltimateSW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> also known as the ''Super''-class Star Destroyer,<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> was the largest model of Star Destroyer ever built by the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="UltimateSW" /> It was usually referred to as a [[Super Star Destroyer]],<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref> and consisted of the sub-models [[Executor I-class Star Dreadnought|''Executor I''-class]]<ref name="Ex I">{{Armada|set=Super Star Destroyer Expansion Pack|cardname=''Executor I''-class Star Dreadnought}}</ref> and [[Executor II-class Star Dreadnought|''Executor II''-class]].<ref name="Ex II">{{Armada|set=Super Star Destroyer Expansion Pack|cardname=''Executor II''-class Star Dreadnought}}</ref> 19,000 [[meter]]s long, it was used as a [[command ship]] and had over 5,000 [[turbolaser]]s and [[ion cannon]]s.<ref name="Starfighter Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref>

The [[Mega-class Star Dreadnought|''Mega''-class Star Dreadnought]], also referred to as the ''Mega''-class Star Destroyer, was the [[capital]] of the [[First Order]] and its [[Supreme Leader]]. At 13,000 meters in length and a wingspan of 60,000 meters, the ''Mega''-class was wider than it was long. The sole example of the model, the ''[[Supremacy]]'', was used by Supreme Leader [[Snoke]] and the [[First Order Navy]] to attack the [[Resistance]].<ref name="TLJ ICS">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref>

====Battlecruisers====
There were multiple examples of Star Destroyers that were classified as [[battlecruiser]]s during [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]]. The [[Maelstrom-class battle cruiser|''Maelstrom''-class battle cruiser]], used by the [[Galactic Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]], was primarily mothballed by the Galactic Empire, and at least one example, the ''[[Simoom]]'', was used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. The ''Maelstrom''-class was considered to be a proto-Star Destroyer, and was armed with [[assault concussion missile launcher]]s, heavy [[cannon]]s, and other weaponry. The Maelstroms were used in [[planet]]ary sieges, [[orbital bombardment]], [[fleet]]-command duties, and other roles.<ref name="Lead by Example">''[[Lead by Example]]''</ref>

[[File:Resurgent-class_Star_Destroyer.png|thumb|right|250px|A ''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer of the First Order]]
The [[Secutor-class Star Destroyer|''Secutor''-class Star Destroyer]], also identified as the ''Secutor''-class battlecarrier, was another example of a battlecruiser in the Star Destroyer design family. A little more than 2 [[kilometer]]s in length, the Secutor was used as a [[carrier]] and [[command ship]] by the Galactic Empire. It was possibly the largest [[starfighter]] dedicated vessel in the [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="Starships and Speeders">''[[Starships and Speeders]]''</ref> The Empire's successor state, the [[First Order]], widely deployed the [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]] (alternatively designated as the ''Resurgent''-class Battlecruiser<ref name="TFA Secret Inside">{{SW|url=news/the-force-awakens-secret-inside-the-secret-academy|text=The ''Force Awakens'' Secret Inside ''The Secret Academy''}}</ref>) during the [[Cold War]]<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref> and the [[First Order-Resistance War]].<ref name="TLJ">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> The Resurgent was a 2,915 meter-long warship that featured advanced weaponry and systems.<ref name="TFA Cross">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref>

According to the [[Anaxes War College System]], the [[Sith Eternal]]'s [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyer]], at 2,406 meters, was a battlecruiser.<ref name="Xyston">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'' establishes that [[warship]]s between 2,000 [[meter]]s and 5,000 meters long were [[battlecruiser]]s. Since the [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyer]] was 2,406 meters in length according to ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'', then it must be classified as a battlecruiser in the system.</ref> The Xyston was a model of Star Destroyer that was based on an upscaled ''Imperial I''-class design. The ''Xyston''-class possessed heavy weaponry, including the [[axial superlaser]] cannon which had the capability of destroying entire planets.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

====Cruisers====
The Republic's [[Acclamator-class transgalactic military assault ship|''Acclamator''-class assault ship]] was a 752 meter-long<ref name="Starfighter Encyclopedia" /> [[cruiser]] that was considered to be a proto-Star Destroyer.<ref name="Lead by Example" /> Its sub-variants were the [[Acclamator I-class Assault Ship|''Acclamator I''-class]]<ref name="Acclamator I">{{Armada|set=Galactic Republic Fleet Starter|cardname=''Acclamator I''-class Assault Ship}}</ref> and the [[Acclamator II-class assault ship|''Acclamator II''-class]].<ref name="Acclamator II">{{Armada|set=Galactic Republic Fleet Starter|cardname=''Acclamator II''-class Assault Ship}}</ref> It was used as a [[carrier]] and [[transport]] for [[troop]]s and vehicles to a planet's surface. The [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]], a class of [[cruiser]]<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> 1,137 meters in length<ref name="Absolutely Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref>, was also referred to as the Republic Attack Cruiser<ref name="Venator DB">{{Databank|republic-attack-cruiser|Republic Attack Cruiser}}</ref> or Jedi cruiser<ref name="ISD DB">{{Databank|imperial-star-destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyer}}</ref> and was considered a proto-Star Destroyer.<ref name="Lead by Example" /> It consisted of two sub-variants, the [[Venator I-class Star Destroyer|''Venator I''-class]]<ref name="V1">{{Armada|set=Venator-class Star Destroyer Expansion Pack|cardname=''Venator I''-class Star Destroyer}}</ref> and the [[Venator II-class Star Destroyer|''Venator II''-class]],<ref name="V2">{{Armada|set=Venator-class Star Destroyer Expansion Pack|cardname=''Venator II''-class Star Destroyer}}</ref> and was extensively used by the Galactic Republic during the Clone Wars and by the early Galactic Empire.<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref>

[[File:ImperialClassStarDestroyer-TSWB.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Imperial I''-class Star Destroyer was a model of cruiser.]]
The successor of the ''Venator''-class,<ref name="ISD DB" /> the 1,600 meter-long<ref name="BMF 20">{{BuildFalconCite|20|Starship Fact File}}</ref> [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]],<ref name="ISD DB" /> was also classified as a cruiser.<ref name="Odyssey">''[[The Odyssey of Star Wars: An Epic Poem]]''</ref> The ''Imperial''-class consisted of the sub-variants [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial I''-class]], [[Imperial II-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial II''-class]], and the [[Interdictor-class Star Destroyer|''Interdictor''-class]].<ref name="BMF 20" /> The ''Imperial''-class became symbols of the Empire's [[New Order]].<ref name="ISD DB" /> The [[Interdictor-class heavy cruiser|''Interdictor''-class heavy cruiser]] was a class of [[heavy cruiser]]<ref name="Starships and Speeders" /> that was also part of the Star Destroyer family of ships used by the Empire.<ref name="Everything Updated">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> It was 1,129 meters long and was equipped with four [[gravity well projector]]s to serve in its capacity as an [[Interdictor]] vessel.<ref name="Starfighter Encyclopedia" /> The [[Onager-class Star Destroyer|''Onager''-class Star Destroyer]] was also classified as a cruiser class, and was equipped with a [[superweapon]] that could destroy targets on the surface of a [[planet]] or entire fleets.<ref name="Starships and Speeders" />

Another cruiser, in accordance with the Anaxes War College System, the [[Gladiator-class Star Destroyer|''Gladiator''-class Star Destroyer]] was the smallest Star Destroyer in the Empire's arsenal at 600 meters in length.<ref name="Gladiator">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'' establishes that [[warship]]s between 400 and 600 meters long were [[cruiser]]s. Since the [[Gladiator-class Star Destroyer|''Gladiator''-class Star Destroyer]] was 600 meters in length according to ''[[Starships and Speeders]]'', then it must be classified as a cruiser in the system.</ref> Despite its size, it was heavily armed and was deployed as a [[patrol ship]] and escort.<ref name="Starships and Speeders" /> It could serve in the capacity of a [[flagship]] for a small [[task force]]<ref name="Friends">''[[Friends Like These]]''</ref> or [[battle group]].<ref name="Nexus">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref> The ''[[Gladiator I]]'' was a sub-variant of the ship.<ref name="Friends" />

====Other examples====
[[File:Victory_II.jpg|thumb|right|280px|A ''Victory II''-class Star Destroyer utilized by the Galactic Empire]]
There were other examples of Star Destroyers that were in service alongside the cruisers, dreadnoughts, and battlecruisers. The [[Imperator-class Star Destroyer|''Imperator''-class Star Destroyer]] was a large, powerful, and multi-functional warship used by the Republic. The ''Imperator''-class saw limited action, and were soon succeeded by the ''Imperial''-class.<ref name="BMF 20" /> The Empire's [[qaz-class Star Destroyer]], armed with multiple batteries, was used by the Empire.<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> The [[Tector-class|''Tector''-class]] was another example that saw service in the Imperial Navy.<ref name="Levers">{{StoryCite|story=The Levers of Power|book=The Rise of the Empire}}</ref>

The [[Victory I-class Star Destroyer|''Victory I''-class Star Destroyer]], deployed by the Republic and subsequent Empire, was another example of the Star Destroyer design. Its successor, the [[Victory II-class Star Destroyer|''Victory II''-class]], sought to fix the multiple design flaws.<ref name="Starships and Speeders" />

==History==
{{Quote|I am looking through the viewscreen, and I believe I see a Star Destroyer. That cannot be. This mission will be easy, you said. But nothing about a Star Destroyer is easy.|Korin Pers, to [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]]|<ref name="Lando 2">[[Lando 2|''Lando'' 2]]</ref>}}
[[File:Imperialattackcruisers.png|thumb|left|250px|A trio of ''Venator''-class Star Destroyers]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Republic Navy|Navy]] fielded a [[fleet]] of [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyers]]. The ''Venator''-class saw action in numerous battles against the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|Confederacy navy]] including the [[Battle of Coruscant]]. Following the [[Proclamation of the New Order|transformation]] of the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire]], the Republic's Star Destroyers were incorporated into the new [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="ROTS" /> Aside from the ''Venator'' and ''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers, other known models in Imperial service included the [[Victory-class Star Destroyer|''Victory'']] and [[Secutor-class Star Destroyer|''Secutor''-class Star Destroyers]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>  The Imperial Navy contained thousands and thousands of Star Destroyers - each one capable of [[orbital bombardment|glassing]] an entire planet - making it history's mightiest starfleet.<ref name="Kernels and Husks">{{StoryCite|story=Kernels and Husks|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref>

During the rebellion and the [[Galactic Civil War]], Imperial Star Destroyers took part in numerous engagements against the various rebel forces that eventually coalesced into the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="The Forgotten Droid">{{Rebels|The Forgotten Droid}}</ref><ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Star Destroyers were deployed during the [[secret mission to Tatooine]],<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> [[Battle of Hoth]],<ref name="TESB">{{Film|V}}</ref> and the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

[[File:StarDestroyer-Fathead.png|thumb|right|300px|The Imperial Star Destroyer]]
Following the events at [[Endor]], the Rebel Alliance's successor government, the [[New Republic]], captured and destroyed numerous Star Destroyers in several engagements including the [[Battle of Theed]],<ref name="SE3">[[Shattered Empire 3|''Shattered Empire'' 3]]</ref> the [[Rebellion on Akiva]],<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> the [[Defense of Kuat]], and the [[Liberation of Kashyyyk]].<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> By [[5 ABY]],<ref name="Life Debt Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]'' to [[5 ABY]].</ref> [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]] estimated that 75% of the Imperial Star Destroyers before Endor had either been destroyed, captured, or lost in "confirmable if curious ways." While trawling through the archives at the [[Hall of Imperial Register]] on [[Coruscant]], Sloane discovered that the remaining 25% had mysteriously disappeared and their purported destruction had been falsified.<ref name="Life Debt" />

Later, Sloane learned that [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Gallius Rax]] secretly commanded Imperial fleets in the [[Almagest]], the [[Recluse's Nebula]], the [[Queluhan Nebula]], the [[Ro-Loo Triangle]], and the [[Inamorata]]. These fleets consisted of hundreds of Star Destroyers and thousands of smaller ships. Following the [[Attack on Chandrila]], Rax ordered the Imperial fleets to assemble above the planet [[Jakku]].<ref name="Life Debt" /> Numerous Star Destroyers, including [[Captain]] [[Ciena Ree]]'s starship ''[[Inflictor]]'', saw action during the [[Battle of Jakku]], the cataclysmic battle that ended the Galactic Civil War in favor of the New Republic.<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref>

[[File:Supremacy.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Mega''-class Star Dreadnought ''Supremacy'' and its escorts.]]
[[34 ABY|Thirty years]] after the Battle of Endor, the barren surface of Jakku was still littered with the wreckage of countless Star Destroyers. These derelict starships were regularly targeted by scavengers<ref name="TFA" /> such as Rey. The First Order, a remnant of the Old Empire, was also known to utilize Star Destroyers as part of its [[First Order Navy|fleet]],<ref name="BTA">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref> such as the First Order's [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyers]], which were inspired by the dagger-shaped design of the Old Empire's vessels.<ref name="TFAVD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> The First Order's leadership, including its [[Supreme Leader]], were stationed aboard the gargantuan [[Mega-class Star Dreadnought|''Mega''-class Star Dreadnought]] ''[[Supremacy]]'', the sole ship of its class.<ref name="Sphero">''[[Star Wars Droids App by Sphero]]''</ref>

[[File:Xyston-classStarDestroyer.png|thumb|right|250px|The ''Xyston''-class Star Destroyer utilized by the Sith Eternal.]]
When the revived [[Darth Sidious]] and his [[Sith Eternal]] [[Sith cultist|cultists]] emerged from [[Exegol]] and assimilated the First Order's military after the death of Supreme Leader [[Snoke]],<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref> the [[Sith Lord]] unveiled his own armada, the [[Final Order]], which was comprised of 1,080 [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyers]].<ref name="VFX-BBC">{{YouTube|video=bDa5h3cj1DU|text=How We brought Carrie Fisher Back|channel=@BBCClick|name=BBC Click}}</ref> The entire fleet was destroyed in the [[Battle of Exegol]] before they could be deployed en masse.<ref name="Episode IX" />

